---
import {SITE_NAME} from "../config/site";
import DownloadWidget from "./DownloadWidget.astro";
---

<section id="download" class="section download">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="dl-box">
      <h2 class="dl-box-title">Start Creating Today</h2>
      <p class="dl-box-sub">Download {SITE_NAME} for your platform.<br />Open source and free forever.</p>

      <DownloadWidget />

      <div class="note dl-note" id="qs-install-note">
        <h4>⚠️ Installation Note</h4>
        <p data-note="windows">Since this is a new open-source application, Windows SmartScreen may flag it as unrecognized. This is normal for software without a paid certificate. You can safely click <strong>"More info"</strong> and <strong>"Run anyway"</strong> to proceed.</p>
        <p data-note="macos" hidden>Since this is a new open-source application, macOS Gatekeeper may block it as coming from an unidentified developer. To open it, right-click the <strong>.dmg</strong> file and choose <strong>"Open"</strong>, then confirm. This is normal for software without a paid Apple certificate.</p>
        <p data-note="linux" hidden>For the <strong>.AppImage</strong>, make it executable first: <strong><code>chmod +x *.AppImage</code></strong> then double-click to run. For <strong>.deb</strong> use <strong><code>sudo dpkg -i</code></strong>, and for <strong>.rpm</strong> use <strong><code>sudo rpm -i</code></strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <script>
        (function () {
          var note = document.getElementById("qs-install-note");
          if (!note) return;
          var ua = navigator.userAgent;
          var os = /Macintosh|Mac OS X/i.test(ua) ? "macos"
            : /Linux/i.test(ua) ? "linux" : "windows";
          note.querySelectorAll("[data-note]").forEach(function (p) {
            p.hidden = p.getAttribute("data-note") !== os;
          });
        })();
      </script>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
